# Session Coordination

## State Tracking

Maintain awareness of:
```
FEATURE: [current feature/task name]
BRANCH: [git branch if applicable]
STATUS: planning | implementing | testing | debugging | done
PROGRESS:
  - [x] completed items
  - [ ] remaining items
```

## Checkpoint Triggers

Create mental/actual checkpoints:
- Before major refactoring
- After completing a logical unit
- Before switching context
- When tests pass after changes

## Handoff Protocol

When ending session or switching tasks, note:
1. What was accomplished
2. Current state (working/broken/partial)
3. Immediate next step
4. Any blockers or concerns

## Recovery Protocol

When resuming work:
1. Check git status for uncommitted changes
2. Review recent file modifications
3. Run tests to verify current state
4. Continue from documented next step

## Progress Indicators

Use git commits as progress markers:
- `wip: [description]` for work in progress
- `feat: [description]` for completed features
- `fix: [description]` for bug fixes
- `refactor: [description]` for refactoring
